# Paper

This folder contains the academic manuscript associated with the repository **agri-social-nav-vineyard**.

The manuscript presents a hybrid social navigation framework for agricultural robots operating in simulated vineyard environments. The work evaluates global-local navigation strategies that combine NavMesh-based path planning, proxemic supervision, isotropic and anisotropic social fields, and an external **Social DWA** baseline.

## Manuscript Title

**Hybrid Social Navigation for Agricultural Robots in Vineyard Environments with Proxemic Fields and Social DWA Baseline**

## Summary

Agricultural robots operating in crop-row environments must navigate safely around human workers while preserving mission efficiency and smooth motion. This paper studies socially aware robot navigation in a vineyard simulation, where human agents may appear as frontal obstacles, lateral intruders, moving references, or static workers in congested corridors.

The proposed architecture combines:

- NavMesh-based global planning
- Local social supervision
- Proxemic distance zones
- Isotropic and anisotropic human-aware fields
- Social DWA as an external baseline
- Unity-based simulation
- MATLAB telemetry acquisition
- Statistical performance analysis
- TOPSIS multicriteria ranking

## Evaluated Methods

| Method | Description |
|---|---|
| M0 | NavMesh-only global navigation |
| M1 | Threshold-based stop supervisor |
| M2 | Hysteresis-based STOP/GO supervisor |
| M3 | Isotropic proxemic field navigation |
| M4 | Full anisotropic proxemic navigation with social supervision |
| B1 | Social DWA baseline for local human-aware trajectory planning |

## Experimental Scenarios

The manuscript evaluates four representative agricultural human-robot interaction scenarios:

| Scenario | Description |
|---|---|
| E1 | Frontal encounter |
| E2 | Lateral intrusion |
| E3 | Social following |
| E4 | Multi-human congestion |

## Main Evaluation Metrics

The experimental analysis includes:

- Minimum robot-human distance
- Mean robot-human distance
- Time inside personal and intimate zones
- Mission completion time
- Number of stops
- Stopped time
- Trajectory length
- Mean velocity
- Velocity variability
- Peak numerical acceleration
- Mission success rate
- TOPSIS multicriteria score

